.TH BLIT-UPDATE-HELPER 8 "2026-11-12" "Blit @VERSION@" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
blit-update-helper \- installs Blit packages uploaded through the API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/lib/blit/bin/blit-update-helper
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B blit-update-helper
is the privileged half of Blit's live update.
A client uploads
.B blit
and
.B blit-compositor
of one version with
.B "PUT /v1/control/update"
and the update token; the server stores each in
.I /var/lib/blit/updates/
and asks the helper to install them.
The server never installs packages itself, so it can run without
root (see
.IR /usr/share/doc/blit/examples/blit-unprivileged.conf ).
.PP
The helper runs as
.BR blit-update-helper.service ,
as root with group blit.
It listens on
.IR /run/blit/update.sock ,
mode 0660, so only the server's group can reach it.
For each request it:
.IP 1. 4
refuses any path that is not a
.I blit-update-*
file directly in
.IR /var/lib/blit/updates/ ;
.IP 2. 4
checks each package's SHA-256 against the one the server sent;
.IP 3. 4
checks that the packages are
.B blit
and, optionally,
.BR blit-compositor ,
at one version;
.IP 4. 4
refuses an update without
.B blit-compositor
when the host has it installed, because
.B blit-compositor
depends on
.B blit
of exactly its own version; if the host does not have it, it is not added;
.IP 5. 4
installs them with one
.BR dpkg (1)
.BR \-\-install ;
.IP 6. 4
removes the staged files, whether it installed them or refused;
.IP 7. 4
after an install, reloads systemd and restarts
.BR blit.service .
.PP
It replies
.B OK
or
.B ERROR
with the reason, which the server returns to the client.
.PP
It takes no arguments and reads no environment.
.SH PROTOCOL
One line per connection, within 3 seconds:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
UPDATE \fIpath\fP \fIsha256\fP [\fIpath\fP \fIsha256\fP]
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A package was installed; systemd starts the helper again.
.TP
.B 1
The socket could not be created.
.TP
.B 2
Arguments were given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/blit/update.sock
The socket.
.TP
.I /var/lib/blit/updates/
Uploaded packages, until the helper has answered.
.TP
.I /etc/blit/update.token
The token the server requires for an update; see
.BR blit.env (5).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR blit (8),
.BR blit.env (5),
.BR dpkg (1)
